<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · British Isles</p><h1 class="st-title">Ui Chennselaig</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 1171 CE (approx.) · capital Ferns</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ruling dynasty of south Leinster, based at Ferns, that produced Diarmait Mac Murchada, whose alliance with the Anglo-Normans changed Irish history.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Uí Chennselaig, 'descendants of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/enna-cennselach">Énna Cennselach</a>', emerged in the 5th and 6th centuries as the leading dynasty of southern <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Leinster</a>, in modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-wexford">Wexford</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-carlow">Carlow</a>. Their royal centre and church were at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferns">Ferns</a>, founded by St <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maedoc-of-ferns">Máedóc</a>. They competed with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ui-dunlainge">Uí Dúnlainge</a> of the north for the kingship of the Kingdom of Leinster.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandub-mac-echach">Brandub mac Echach</a>, who defeated the high king at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dun-bolg">Dún Bolg</a> in 598, was their most famous early king. After a long period of northern dominance, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-mael-na-mbo">Diarmait mac Máel na mBó</a> revived their fortunes in the 11th century, taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dublin">Dublin</a> and ruling much of southern Ireland. The family of his descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macmurrough-dynasty">Meic Murchada</a> or MacMurroughs, became the kings of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Leinster</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diarmait-mac-murchada">Diarmait Mac Murchada</a>, driven out in 1166, brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-normans">Anglo-Norman</a> knights to Ireland. On his death in 1171 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-de-clare-2nd-earl-of-pembroke">Strongbow</a> took <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-leinster">Leinster</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macmurrough-dynasty">MacMurrough Kavanaghs</a> later revived as independent lords in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-wexford">Wexford</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-carlow">Carlow</a>, resisting English rule until the 16th century.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 450 CE – 1171 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">British Isles</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:68.66%;width:14.35%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 CE – 1171 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ferns</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Brandub mac Echach, Diarmait mac Máel na mBó, Diarmait Mac Murchada</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Irish, later Middle Irish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/ireland">Ireland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Uí Chennselaig, Hy Kinsella</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=810&amp;focus=ui-chennselaig" aria-label="Ui Chennselaig on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4534 364 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ui Chennselaig lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4854 620L4854 620"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4854 620h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4854 620h0"/><path